SDL3 with its DOS port (VESA, Sound Blaster, keyboard, mouse), for FLT.EXE
(../Makefile) and CHIRP.EXE (../chirp/Makefile): exact copies of the files of
github.com/jasonbrianhall/SDLPoPDOS (main, commit d1ef79a) that its DOS build
compiles into libSDL3.a, from its msdos/ folder. Nothing here needs an
SDLPoPDOS checkout; the build uses these files only.

  SDL3/          SDL3 3.5.0 (libsdl.org, commit 4ca1b1c, zlib license:
                 SDL3/LICENSE.txt): the 206 sources in SOURCES, the headers
                 they use, and the public headers (SDL3/include/SDL3)
  sdl3-config/   SDLPoPDOS's generated SDL_build_config.h and SDL_revision.h
  sdl3.mk        the rules both Makefiles include: SOURCES compiled with
                 SDLPoPDOS's SDL_CFLAGS into build/libSDL3.a

SOURCES is SDLPoPDOS's SDL_SRCS. The rest of SDL's tree (other platforms,
tests) is left out. To update: copy the same files from a newer SDLPoPDOS
msdos/ over these (and its SDL_SRCS into SOURCES), and change the commit
above. ../chirp/cwsdpmi has CWSDPMI r7's stub (CWSDSTUB.EXE), its
documentation and license, from SDLPoPDOS's msdos/cwsdpmi.

Changed here (marked "felixterminal:" in the source; keep them when
updating, or send them to SDLPoPDOS):
  SDL3/src/video/dos/SDL_dosmouse.c, SDL_dosevents.c: the mouse wheel,
                 where the driver has CuteMouse's WheelAPI (INT 33h 11h);
                 and clicks made between two polls (INT 33h 5's press
                 counts), which were lost: a quick double-click was none.
